# Spec: [NAME]

## Goal
[A clear, concrete goal. Avoid negations - write WHAT should be done, not what should NOT be done.]

## Requirements
- [ ] Requirement 1
- [ ] Requirement 2
- [ ] Requirement 3

## Technical Stack
- [Language/framework]
- [Database if relevant]
- [Test framework]

## Iteration Instructions
1. Read spec and current code
2. Implement next unfulfilled requirement
3. Run tests
4. If tests fail, fix
5. Mark requirement as done
6. If all requirements done, output completion promise

## Success Criterion
When ALL requirements are fulfilled and tests pass, output exactly:
<promise>DONE</promise>

---

## Tips for good specs (from tutorial)

**Do:**
- One goal per spec
- Clear, measurable requirements
- Include test instructions
- Use checkboxes for progress

**Avoid:**
- Negations ("don't do X")
- Vague requirements ("make it good")
- Multiple goals in same spec
- Too large tasks (split them up!)

> "A bad spec is 10,000 lines of crap." — Geoffrey Huntley
